course: dictionary
lesson: 8244
title: Two meanings, one word: rhesus
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around the word. «The Monkey King is a story hero, but rhesus macaques really live wild in China and quickly learn to grab food and phones from tourists.» The clues are live wild, grab food and tourists, so rhesus here names an animal: a monkey.
explain: In science lessons, rhesus means something about blood. «Rhesus positive» and «rhesus negative» show the plus or minus in blood types like O+ and A−. Blood is rhesus positive if it has the rhesus factor, a protein on the red blood cells, and rhesus negative if it does not.
explain: Always check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. "Rhesus macaques" fits with "monkeys", so the monkey meaning works. "Rhesus negative" only makes sense as a blood type, so the context tells you which meaning to use.
fact: A rhesus monkey, also called a rhesus macaque, is a small brown monkey from Asia with a reddish face.
fact: The rhesus factor is a protein found on red blood cells.
fact: Blood is rhesus positive if it has the rhesus factor, and rhesus negative if it does not.
fact: The rhesus factor was named after experiments with rhesus monkeys.
fact: Rhesus monkeys live in India, China and nearby places, often in cities and temples.
exercise: «...rhesus macaques really live wild in China...» What are rhesus macaques? | *A small brown monkey from Asia with a reddish face | A type of red bus | A kind of fish that lives in deep seas | A large grey bird from Africa
exercise: In science, «rhesus positive» is a blood type. What does rhesus positive mean? | Blood with no red cells at all | Blood that is very cold | *Blood that has the rhesus factor protein on its red blood cells | Blood that comes only from monkeys
exercise: Which word in the sentence tells you where rhesus macaques live wild? | Monkey | Hero | *China | Tourists
test: In the blood type A−, the minus sign means what? | Rhesus positive, so the blood has the rhesus factor | A rhesus monkey from Asia | The blood is very old | *Rhesus negative, so the blood does not have the rhesus factor
test: Blood with no rhesus factor is called what? | Rhesus monkey | Rhesus positive | *Rhesus negative | Rhesus macaque
exam: Which sentence uses rhesus to mean a blood type? | The rhesus monkeys were grabbing food from the tourists | *She is rhesus negative, so the doctor chose blood without the rhesus factor for her | The rhesus monkey is small and brown | The rhesus macaque has a reddish face and climbs trees
